=== sort() Function Tests ===

1. Simple numeric array:
   Original:  [3, 1, 4, 1, 11, 5, 9, 2, 6]
   Original unchanged:  [3, 1, 4, 1, 11, 5, 9, 2, 6]
   Sorted result:  [1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11]

2. String array:
   Original:  ["zebra", "apple", "banana", "cherry"]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra", "apple", "banana", "cherry"]
   Sorted result:  ["apple", "banana", "cherry", "zebra"]

3. Mixed types (numbers before strings):
   Original:  ["hello", 42, "world", 10, "test", 5]
   Original unchanged:  ["hello", 42, "world", 10, "test", 5]
   Sorted result:  [5, 10, 42, "hello", "test", "world"]

4. Source array unchanged:
   Source before:  [5, 2, 8, 1, 9]
   Source after:  [5, 2, 8, 1, 9]
   Sorted result:  [1, 2, 5, 8, 9]

5. Associative array (string keys):
   Original:  ["zebra" => 1, "apple" => 1, "banana" => 1]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra" => 1, "apple" => 1, "banana" => 1]
   Sorted result:  [1, 1, 1]

6. Associative array (numeric keys):
   Original:  [10 => "ten", 2 => "two", 5 => "five", 1 => "one"]
   Original unchanged:  [10 => "ten", 2 => "two", 5 => "five", 1 => "one"]
   Sorted result:  ["five", "one", "ten", "two"]

7. Empty array:
   Original:  []
   Sorted result:  []

8. Single element:
   Original:  [42]
   Sorted result:  [42]

9. Already sorted array:
   Original:  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
   Original unchanged:  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
   Sorted result:  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

10. Reverse sorted array:
   Original:  [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
   Original unchanged:  [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
   Sorted result:  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

11. Case sensitivity (mixed case):
   Original:  ["abc", "aBc", "ABC", "Abc", "aBC", "abC"]
   Original unchanged:  ["abc", "aBc", "ABC", "Abc", "aBC", "abC"]
   Sorted result:  ["ABC", "Abc", "aBC", "aBc", "abC", "abc"]

12. Case sensitivity (lowercase vs uppercase):
   Original:  ["zebra", "ZEBRA", "apple", "APPLE", "banana", "BANANA"]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra", "ZEBRA", "apple", "APPLE", "banana", "BANANA"]
   Sorted result:  ["APPLE", "BANANA", "ZEBRA", "apple", "banana", "zebra"]

13. Case sensitivity (same letters, different cases):
   Original:  ["Hello", "hello", "HELLO", "hElLo", "HeLlO"]
   Original unchanged:  ["Hello", "hello", "HELLO", "hElLo", "HeLlO"]
   Sorted result:  ["HELLO", "HeLlO", "Hello", "hElLo", "hello"]

14. Case sensitivity (single character differences):
   Original:  ["a", "A", "b", "B", "c", "C"]
   Original unchanged:  ["a", "A", "b", "B", "c", "C"]
   Sorted result:  ["A", "B", "C", "a", "b", "c"]

15. Case sensitivity (with numbers and mixed case):
   Original:  ["test1", "Test1", "TEST1", "test2", "Test2", "TEST2"]
   Original unchanged:  ["test1", "Test1", "TEST1", "test2", "Test2", "TEST2"]
   Sorted result:  ["TEST1", "TEST2", "Test1", "Test2", "test1", "test2"]

16. Multidimensional array (sort values):
   Original:  ["12" => 30, "45" => 10, "23" => 20]
   Original unchanged:  ["12" => 30, "45" => 10, "23" => 20]
   Sorted result:  [10, 20, 30]

17. Multidimensional array (string values):
   Original:  ["12" => "zebra", "45" => "apple", "23" => "banana"]
   Original unchanged:  ["12" => "zebra", "45" => "apple", "23" => "banana"]
   Sorted result:  ["apple", "banana", "zebra"]

18. Multidimensional array (mixed types):
   Original:  ["12" => "hello", "45" => 42, "23" => "world", "34" => 10]
   Original unchanged:  ["12" => "hello", "45" => 42, "23" => "world", "34" => 10]
   Sorted result:  [10, 42, "hello", "world"]

19. Three-dimensional array:
   Original:  ["123" => 50, "111" => 10, "222" => 30, "121" => 20]
   Original unchanged:  ["123" => 50, "111" => 10, "222" => 30, "121" => 20]
   Sorted result:  [10, 20, 30, 50]

20. Multidimensional array (string indices):
   Original:  ["row1col1" => 100, "row2col1" => 50, "row1col2" => 75]
   Original unchanged:  ["row1col1" => 100, "row2col1" => 50, "row1col2" => 75]
   Sorted result:  [50, 75, 100]

21. Nested arrays
   Original:  [[5, 3], [9, 1], [2, 8], [11, 2]]
   Original unchanged:  [[5, 3], [9, 1], [2, 8], [11, 2]]
   Sorted result:  [[2, 8], [5, 3], [9, 1], [11, 2]]

=== All sort() Tests Complete ===
